rˆ␀␀␀Ú_ASSERT_NEVER_REPR_MAX_LENGTHéd␀␀␀r,␀␀␀ry␀␀c␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀ó˜␀␀␀—␀t␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀|␀¦␀␀«␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀}t␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀|¦␀␀«␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀t␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀k␀␀␀␀r|dt␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀…␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀dz␀␀␀}t␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀d|›␀¦␀␀«␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀‚)a1␀␀Assert to the type checker that a line of code is unreachable.

        Example::

            def int_or_str(arg: int | str) -> None:
                match arg:
                    case int():
                        print("It's an int")
                    case str():
                        print("It's a str")
                    case _:
                        assert_never(arg)

        If a type checker finds that a call to assert_never() is
        reachable, it will emit an error.

        At runtime, this throws an exception when called.

